-- title:
--   Error bound for the segmented inverse of the resampling system (real form)
-- statement:
--   Let $s\le t$ be lengths with $s>0$, let $\alpha\ge 2$ be the Gaussian parameter and assume $x=\alpha^2\theta=\alpha^2(t-s)/s\ge 3$ (`xθ s t α`). Let $B$ be a valid block structure (`BlocksOK s t B`: wrap-free runs partitioning $[0,s)$ with coupling width $w=B.w$) whose blocks all have length at most $\lambda$, and let $T$ be precomputed fixed-point tables of precision $P$ accurate to $E\ge 0$ ulps with per-block constants bounded by $D_m$ (`TabOK P s t α B T E Dm`). Put $G=D_m\,((\lambda+1)E+1)\,(B_u+1)\,(\lambda+1)\,(2w+1)\,(|J|+1)^2$ (`segG`), where $|J|$ is the number of near-boundary positions of the block structure. Let $U:\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z$ be a fixed-point input with $|U_i/2^P|\le B_u$ ($B_u\ge0$) for $i<s$, and let $v,w:\mathbb N\to\mathbb R$ satisfy $|w_i|\le W_m$, the resampling system $N w = v$ (`NxR s t α w i = v i`) for $i<s$, and $|U_i/2^P - v_i|\le\varepsilon_{in}$. If $1000\,G\le 2^P$, then for every $i<s$ the output of the segmented inverse `segInv P T B U` satisfies
--   $$\Bigl|\frac{\mathrm{segInv}(U)_i}{2^P}-w_i\Bigr|\le \frac{60\,G}{2^P}+3\cdot 4e^{-\pi\alpha^2 w(w+1)}(B_u+1)+\tfrac87\varepsilon_{in}.$$
--
